# Frontend Standards

See also: **compact-code** rule — prefer minimal, focused diffs. **dashboard-layout** rule — page stack, card grid, spacing.

## Mobile-First Responsive Design

- Write base styles for mobile, then enhance with `sm:`, `md:`, `lg:`, `xl:` breakpoints.
- Test layouts at 320px, 768px, and 1280px minimum widths.
- Use Tailwind CSS utilities; avoid custom CSS unless a pattern is reused 3+ times.
- Navigation must collapse to a Sheet drawer below `lg` breakpoint.

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — mobile-first
<div className="flex flex-col gap-6 md:flex-row md:gap-12">

// ❌ BAD — desktop-first overrides
<div className="flex flex-row max-md:flex-col">
```

## Performance & CLS Prevention

- Use `next/image` for all raster images with explicit `width`, `height`, and `sizes`.
- Use `next/font` for fonts; never load fonts via `<link>` tags.
- Reserve space for dynamic content to prevent layout shift.
- Prefer CSS/SVG for icons and UI mockups over heavy image assets.
- Mark client-only components with `"use client"` only when necessary.

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD
import Image from "next/image";
<Image src="/hero.png" alt="Dashboard" width={800} height={600} priority sizes="(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 50vw" />
```

## TypeScript & Component Structure

- Use strict TypeScript; no `any` unless unavoidable with a comment explaining why.
- Co-locate landing page sections in `components/landing/`.
- Export one primary component per file; use named exports for sub-components.
- Props interfaces should be explicit and exported when reused.

## Semantic HTML & Accessibility

- Use `<header>`, `<nav>`, `<main>`, `<section>`, `<footer>` landmarks.
- Every interactive element must be keyboard-accessible.
- Images and icons need descriptive `alt` text or `aria-hidden="true"` for decorative elements.
- Maintain WCAG AA color contrast ratios.

## Branding

- Import product name and copy from `@/lib/brand` — never hardcode the product name in components.
- Use `BRAND.name`, `BRAND.tagline`, and helper functions like `brandCopyright()` for all user-facing branding.

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD
import { BRAND } from "@/lib/brand";
<h1>{BRAND.tagline}</h1>

// ❌ BAD
<h1>DocuCredit AI</h1>
```

## API & Security

- Browser calls **same-origin** `/api/*` only — use `apiClient` / helpers from `@/lib/api`.
- Backend URL is configured via **`API_PROXY_TARGET`** (server-only). Never use `NEXT_PUBLIC_` for API URLs.
- `API_PROXY_TARGET` is **required in production** (enforced at build time).
- All `fetch` calls use `credentials: "same-origin"`.

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD
import { login } from "@/lib/api";
await login({ email, password }); // → POST /api/auth/login (proxied server-side)

// ❌ BAD — exposes backend URL in client bundle, requires CORS
fetch("https://api.example.com/api/auth/login", { ... });
```


- UI primitives live in `components/ui/`; do not modify Radix behavior without reason.
- Use `cn()` from `@/lib/utils` for conditional class merging.
- Extend variants via `class-variance-authority`, not inline style objects.

## Dashboard CSS (`styles/pages/dashboard.css`)

- Every `@apply` must live inside a selector block `{ ... }` — orphaned `@apply` lines cause `Missing opening {` build failures.
- After fixing CSS errors, restart dev server and run `rm -rf .next` if Turbopack still reports stale errors.
- Prefer plain CSS for `calc()` / complex values instead of arbitrary `@apply` utilities when builds fail mysteriously.
